# ToDoTest frontend implementation

Use this rule together with `frontend-nuxt.mdc`, `design-system.mdc` and
`api-conventions.mdc`. The detailed reference is
`docs/frontend-implementation-plan.md`.

## Source of truth

- ToDoTest technical standards have priority over copied code from Navision.
- Navision is a reference for component structure, naming and reusable UI patterns.
- Preserve the small-project scope. Do not add abstractions without real reusable responsibility.
- Do not modify unrelated files.

## Stack

- Nuxt 3 and Vue 3.
- TypeScript strict mode.
- Composition API and `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- SCSS and CSS custom properties for design tokens.
- Typed API layer.
- One Nuxt application for public routes and `/admin`.
- Separate public and admin layouts and route middleware.
- Vitest, Playwright, ESLint, Prettier and CI checks.

Do not introduce JavaScript-only components, Tailwind, mixins or a global event bus.

## Component naming

Keep the Navision naming pattern:

| Prefix | Responsibility | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| `Ui` | Low-level visual primitive | `UiButton`, `UiInput`, `UiTable`, `UiSheet` |
| `El` | Generic composed element | `ElForm`, `ElSelect`, `ElInputCalendar` |
| `Pt` | Reusable interface pattern | `PtTable`, `PtFilter`, `PtTabs`, `PtCardInfo` |
| `Tm` | Large template, layout or sheet | `TmSidebar`, `TmHeader`, `TmTodoListSheet` |
| `use` | Typed composable | `useTableData`, `useAdminSession` |
| `format` | Pure formatting helper | `formatDate`, `formatTaskPriority` |

- Component filenames use PascalCase.
- Component tags in templates use kebab-case.
- Feature components keep the layer prefix, for example `PtTaskCard`, `PtTaskFilters`,
  `TmAdminDashboard` and `TmAdminTaskSheet`.
- `Ui` components must not know business API or domain-specific endpoints.

## Directory structure

Prefer this structure:

```text
frontend/
├── pages/
├── layouts/
├── middleware/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/
│   ├── elements/
│   ├── patterns/
│   │   └── filters/
│   └── templates/
│       ├── layouts/
│       └── sheets/
├── composables/
├── services/
│   └── api/
├── types/
├── utils/
├── plugins/
├── assets/styles/
└── tests/
```

Layer responsibilities:

- `components/ui`: primitive visuals and interaction contracts.
- `components/elements`: generic composition of UI primitives.
- `components/patterns`: reusable table, filter, tabs and information patterns.
- `components/templates`: layouts, sidebars, headers and sheets for large screen sections.
- `pages`: route orchestration and page-level composition.
- `composables`: typed reusable behavior with a real shared owner.
- `services/api`: the only place where endpoint paths are defined.
- `utils`: pure functions without Vue or API state.

## Vue file style

Use this SFC order:

```text
template
script setup lang="ts"
style scoped lang="scss"
```

Use this script order:

```text
imports
props/emits
composables/stores
state
computed
watchers/lifecycle
handlers
```

Use props, emits and slots for communication. Keep local UI state local. Use Pinia only when
multiple independent features share state with a clear owner.

Do not use `any`, non-null assertions or ignored errors without a documented reason.

## Typed API layer

UI components and pages must not construct endpoint URLs. Use typed methods from `services/api`.

Recommended namespaces:

```ts
api.profiles
api.todoLists
api.tasks
api.tags
api.admin.auth
api.admin.dashboard
api.admin.users
api.admin.tasks
```

API rules:

- URL paths use kebab-case.
- JSON fields use snake_case.
- TypeScript methods and local variables use camelCase.
- Requests use `credentials: 'include'`.
- Admin login first requests the CSRF cookie.
- Send `X-XSRF-TOKEN` from the `XSRF-TOKEN` cookie for mutating admin requests.
- Handle 401, 403, 419, 422 and 204 centrally.
- Keep one consistent response shape. Do not silently unwrap different endpoints differently.
- Map `{ errors: { field: string[] } }` to form fields through a shared utility.
- Do not expose internal exception details or stack traces.
- Update API types and tests when the backend contract changes.

The demo profile and admin session are different concerns:

```text
useDemoProfile()
useAdminSession()
```

Do not copy Navision Bearer-token `useAuth` into this project.

## Public and admin zones

Keep one Nuxt application with separate zones:

```text
layouts/default.vue
layouts/admin.vue
middleware/profile.ts
middleware/admin-auth.ts
pages/admin/login.vue
pages/admin/index.vue
```

Admin middleware must load the current session, redirect unauthenticated users to the admin login,
preserve the intended route when practical and handle expired sessions explicitly.

Authorization must remain enforced by the backend. Hiding a button is only a UX detail.

## Reusable patterns

Prefer these Navision patterns after adapting them to TypeScript and SCSS:

- `PtTable`: typed columns, slots, sorting, pagination, loading and empty state.
- `PtFilter`: typed filter config, debounce, query synchronization and reset.
- `PtTabs`: route or model-backed tabs.
- `PtCardInfo`: typed information rows with custom slots.
- `UiSheet` and `UiModal`: controlled visibility, overlay, Escape, footer and nested panels.
- `TmSidebar`, `TmHeader` and `TmMenu`: the base for the admin shell.
- `useTableData`: reusable table query state and pagination behavior.
- `useClickOutside`: dropdown and popover behavior.
- `normalizeApiPagination`: one pagination adapter.

The table column contract should remain typed and explicit:

```ts
interface TableColumn<Row> {
    field: string
    header: string
    sortable?: boolean
    align?: 'left' | 'center' | 'right'
    value?: (row: Row) => unknown
    format?: (value: unknown, row: Row) => string
}
```

For filters use explicit types such as `input`, `select`, `multi-select`, `date` and
`button-group`. Todo task filters include `search`, `status`, `priority`, `tag_id`, `due`, `sort`,
`direction`, `page` and `per_page`.

## Porting Navision components

Treat Navision code as a starting point, not as drop-in code.

For every ported component:

1. Rewrite JavaScript props, emits and slots as strict TypeScript.
2. Remove Tailwind classes and move visual values to ToDoTest SCSS tokens.
3. Replace Navision API and domain data with ToDoTest contracts.
4. Check SSR and client-only behavior.
5. Add ARIA attributes and visible keyboard focus.
6. Check Escape, focus trap, focus return and body scroll for overlays.
7. Add a focused unit test.
8. Run lint, format check, typecheck and tests.

Recommended porting order:

1. `UiButton`, `UiInput`, `UiBadge`, `UiSpinner`, `UiTable`.
2. `UiCard`, `UiEmpty`, `UiPagination`.
3. `UiSheet`, `UiModal`, `UiPopover`.
4. `ElInput`, `ElSelect`, `ElForm`, `ElInputWrapper`.
5. `PtTable`, `PtFilter`, `PtTabs`, `PtCardInfo`.
6. `TmSidebar`, `TmHeader`, `TmMenu`.
7. Todo and admin templates.

Do not copy directly:

- Navision Bearer authentication and `useAuth`.
- `useLibrary` and Navision status maps.
- Navision business sheets.
- Tailwind configuration and Tailwind-only dependencies.
- JavaScript-only helpers.
- Silent catches or inconsistent response unwrapping.

## SCSS and design tokens

Use the existing ToDoTest token structure:

```text
assets/styles/
├── tokens/
├── themes/
├── _mixins.scss
├── _reset.scss
└── main.scss
```

Components consume semantic variables such as:

```text
--color-primary
--color-surface
--color-surface-muted
--color-text
--color-text-muted
--color-border
--color-danger
--color-focus
```

- Do not hardcode brand hex colors in components.
- Do not hardcode static spacing, radii or shadows in components.
- Do not use static inline styles.
- Use scoped SCSS for non-trivial components.
- Use BEM-style class names for non-trivial component styles.
- Keep public and admin zones on the same token system.
- Include hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, invalid and loading states.
- Preserve visible keyboard focus and accessible contrast.

## UI states and domain rules

Every screen and request must model explicit initial, loading, success, empty, error and disabled
states. Also model project-specific read-only states:

- Blocked profiles remain readable but cannot mutate data.
- Archived lists remain readable but their tasks cannot be changed.
- Admins may edit and delete tasks in blocked profiles and archived lists.
- Hard task deletion requires explicit confirmation.
- A successful mutation replaces local data with the returned API Resource when possible.
- HTTP 403 must produce a clear read-only state where the contract requires it.

## Testing and CI

Use unit tests for pure logic, API mappers, pagination, filters and form errors. Use component tests
for shared tables, filters and overlays. Use Playwright for the main public flow and an admin smoke flow.

Required commands:

```bash
npm run lint
npm run format:check
npm run typecheck
npm run test:run
npm run test:e2e
npm run build
```

The full quality path must remain available through `make check` and CI.

## Implementation sequence

Implement vertical slices in this order:

1. UX map, navigation, wireframes and UI state matrix.
2. Frontend foundation, layouts, middleware, API client, types and shared UI primitives.
3. Demo profile selection and restoration.
4. Todo list creation, rename, archive, restore and active/archived tabs.
5. Task and tag creation, editing, filters, sorting, deadlines and read-only states.
6. Admin login, dashboard, users, lists and task management.
7. Responsive, accessibility, tests and final production build.

After every TODO or implementation slice:

- stop before starting the next slice;
- report changed files and decisions;
- report checks and their exact results;
- surface uncertainties and API assumptions;
- wait for explicit user confirmation before continuing.

## Definition of done

A frontend slice is complete only when:

- all API calls use the typed API layer;
- component names follow `Ui`, `El`, `Pt` and `Tm` layers;
- styles use SCSS tokens;
- loading, empty, error and disabled states exist;
- 422 errors are mapped to fields;
- 403 read-only behavior is visible;
- HTTP 204 is handled correctly;
- mutation results update local state from the returned Resource;
- relevant unit and e2e tests exist;
- lint, format check, typecheck, tests and build pass.
